CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 4
Every victim of gender-based violence and child victim of violence has the right to obtain:
a. protection for personal safety, family, and property, as well as freedom from threats related to testimony that will be, is being, or has been given;
b. participation in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
c. information regarding case developments and court decisions;
d. services that are fast, appropriate, comfortable, and in accordance with needs;
e. recovery and social reintegration;
f. legal assistance, psychological assistance, spiritual guidance, economic assistance, social assistance, and an interpreter.

Article 3
(1) The objectives of implementing protection for victims of gender-based violence and children are:
a. to prevent all forms of gender-based violence and violence against children, occurring within the household and/or community;
b. to provide protection;
c. to provide legal assistance;
d. to pursue recovery and social reintegration; and/or
e. to increase community participation.
(2) The objectives of implementing protection for victims of gender-based violence and children as referred to in paragraph (1), include the aspects of:
a. prevention;
b. services and assistance;
c. reunification; and
d. empowerment.

Article 17
The provision of services and assistance to victims of gender-based violence and children, is carried out with the principles of:
a. fast, safe, and empathetic;
b. guarantee of confidentiality;
c. easily accessible; and
d. free of charge.

Article 20
(1) Forms of Reunification provided to victims of gender-based violence and children are as follows:
a. return;
b. social reintegration.
(2) Return services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a include:
a. carrying out coordination with relevant agencies;
b. carrying out the process of returning the victim; and
c. providing protection until reaching the victim's destination.
(3) Social reintegration services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b include:
a. assistance in the process of reunification with the victim's family;
b. providing information to the local community for the victim's reunification with their environment;
c. providing assurance that the family and community are ready to accept the victim back; and
d. carrying out economic empowerment.

Article 24
(1) In order to achieve the objectives of implementing protection against gender-based violence and violence against children as referred to in Article 3, the Regional Government cooperates with: a. the Government;
b. the Provincial Government;
c. other regency/city governments; and
d. the community.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of violence;
c. return and social reintegration; and
d. provision of evidence and witnesses, and follow-up in accordance with applicable law.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be implemented in accordance with laws and regulations.

CHAPTER IX
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 28
(1) The community may participate in efforts to implement protection against acts of gender-based violence and violence against children.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), may be carried out by individuals or organizations.
(3) Community participation in the implementation of protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Violence Against Children may be carried out through:
a. providing protection for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
b. providing emergency assistance;
c. providing advocacy to victims and/or the community regarding the handling of cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders;
e. conveying information to the competent authorities related to cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
f. fostering local wisdom with the principles of non-discrimination and best interests of victims in handling gender-based violence and violence against children;
g. organizing strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based violence and violence against children;
h. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based violence and violence against children.

Article 14
(1) The Regional Government conducts empowerment and awareness-raising for families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling to prevent the occurrence of criminal acts of gender-based violence and violence against children.
(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness-raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government undertakes efforts as follows:
a. increasing the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
c. opening employment opportunities;
d. building community participation and concern to implement prevention and protection against acts of gender-based violence and violence against children;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building cooperative networks with law enforcement officers, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about gender and children; and
g. opening complaint posts for protection against acts of gender-based violence and violence against children.

Article 21
(1) The Regional Government is obligated to conduct empowerment of victims of acts of violence.
(2) The empowerment of victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented by the Women, Children and Adolescent Protection Institution.
(3) In conducting empowerment of victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall formulate empowerment programs in the economic field, which include:
a. procuring the necessary requirements for entrepreneurship training for victims of acts of violence, in order to improve business knowledge, attitude, and skills;
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;
c. providing assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large enterprises, as well as financial institutions to develop the businesses of victims of acts of violence;
e. endeavoring to facilitate the provision of capital for victims of acts of violence; and
f. expanding information access and promoting the products of victims of acts of violence.
(4) In conducting empowerment of victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may establish cooperation with job training institutions organized by the private sector.

Article 7
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include:
 a. implementing protection policies against gender-based violence and violence against children as determined by the government;
 b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for protection against gender-based violence and violence against children;
 c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence;
 d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and violence against children;
 e. allocating a budget for the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and violence against children in accordance with regional financial capacity; and
 f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and violence against children.
(2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the regional government establishes action programs and activities for protection against gender-based violence and violence against children in 1 (one) Regional Action Plan as a basis for SKPD in implementing protection against gender-based violence and violence against children.
(3) Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be regulated by a Mayor Regulation.

Article 15
(1) Efforts to prevent the occurrence of gender-based and child violence as referred to in Article 14, shall be implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. public order and security; and
g. planning.
(2) Prevention of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

